Assertions:
[REL] WEEK_1 count == WEEK_0 count + 1, MTD_1 count == MTD_0 count + 1 and YTD_1 count == YTD_0 count + 1 {SPEC}
[REL] YTD_1 total - YTD_0 total == ORDER_TOTAL (same currency as the dashboard) {SPEC}
[REL] AOV_1 == YTD_1 total / YTD_1 count, rounded as displayed {SPEC}
[REL] ROW1_1 == ORDER_NO {SPEC}
[STATE] the new order is counted in the same session, without waiting for the five-minute cache window (an order save expires the buyer's cache) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] after Save and reload the 'Orders placed · WEEK' card is absent and listed under the hidden stats, the other three cards remain {SPEC}
[DOM] after Reset and Save and a reload the cards captioned 'Orders placed · WEEK', 'Orders placed · MTD', 'Orders placed · YTD' and 'Avg order value' are all rendered in that order {SPEC}
[NETWORK] one GetOrderStatistics request per page load carries all the visible cards' slices; no GetOrders request is repeated for the same page load {OBSERVED}

[REL] WEEK, MTD and YTD count AFTER == count WITH - 1 and each total AFTER == total WITH - ORDER_TOTAL {SPEC}
[REL] ROWS_AFTER differs from ROWS_WITH in exactly one row, the one of ORDER_NO, whose status changed to Cancelled - the order that left the cards is ORDER_NO and no other order changed {SPEC}
[STATE] the cancelled order leaves all three cards in the same session, without a five-minute lag {SPEC}
[DOM] ORDER_NO is still listed in 'My recent orders' with status Cancelled (the list shows every status) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the tab row of 'My recent orders' offers a 'Cancelled' tab labelled with the status name only (no count); clicking it lists ORDER_NO and only orders with status Cancelled {OBSERVED}

[REL] WEEK period from == the UTC instant of Monday 2026-11-09 00:00 Europe/Berlin and its to is at or after 2026-11-09 23:59:59.999 Berlin - on a Monday the week window is today only {SPEC}
[REL] MTD period from == the UTC instant of 2026-11-01 00:00 Berlin; YTD period from == the UTC instant of 2026-01-01 00:00 Berlin {SPEC}
[REL] the WEEK comparison (previous) window covers the 7 days before the current window's from, ending 1 ms before it, and begins on a Monday {SPEC}
[COUNT] GetOrderStatistics requests per page load == 1 {OBSERVED}
[REL] no window bound is a UTC midnight (00:00:00.000Z) unless that instant equals the local midnight above {SPEC}

[REL] the WEEK window of each context contains PLACED_AT (from <= PLACED_AT <= to) {SPEC}
[REL] WEEK_A == WEEK_A0 + 1, MTD_A == MTD_A0 + 1, WEEK_B == WEEK_B0 + 1 and MTD_B == MTD_B0 + 1 - an order placed today is in today's week and month wherever the buyer is, and counted exactly once {SPEC}
[REL] the date shown for ORDER_NO (row 1) in 'My recent orders' equals the buyer's local date of PLACED_AT in each context (list and cards agree on the day) {OBSERVED}
[REL] the two contexts send DIFFERENT window bounds (the bounds follow the browser time zone) {OBSERVED}

[DOM] on the seed day no card renders a change line (the previous span is empty, so the percent is null) - not '+0%', not '0%', not 'NaN%' and not 'Infinity%' {SPEC}
[DOM] CHG_WEEK reads '-100% vs last week' with a down arrow in the negative colour: count 0 now against the seed orders one week earlier {SPEC} {OBSERVED}
[DOM] CHG_MTD reads '-100% vs last month' with the negative styling {SPEC}
[DOM] CHG_YTD reads '-100% vs last year' with the negative styling {SPEC}
[FORMAT] every change text matches /^[-+]\d+(\.\d+)?% vs last (week|month|year)$/ or is absent - never NaN, Infinity or a bare sign {SPEC}
[REL] the change is computed on the ORDER COUNT: the card never shows a revenue percentage (the revenue changes by a different amount on the same data, see the API row) {SPEC}

[REL] ORG_B differs from ORG_A and every card figure under ORG_B differs from A_* or is zero - the previous company's cached figures are not carried over {SPEC}
[DOM] under the organization with no orders the cards read 0 and $0.00 with no change text, and the list shows 'There are no orders yet' with a 'Continue browsing' action {OBSERVED}
[REL] A2_* == A_* - switching back restores the first company's figures {SPEC}
[NETWORK] a GetOrderStatistics request is issued after each switch (the page does not reuse the previous organization's response) {SPEC}

